## Pre-built Themes

Clarity Chat includes 11 professionally designed themes:

1. **Default** - Clean, professional design
2. **Ocean Blue** - Calm, trustworthy blue palette
3. **Forest Green** - Natural, balanced green tones
4. **Sunset Orange** - Warm, energetic orange hues
5. **Royal Purple** - Elegant, sophisticated purple
6. **Cherry Red** - Bold, attention-grabbing red
7. **Midnight** - Dark, modern aesthetic
8. **Pastel** - Soft, gentle pastel colors
9. **High Contrast** - Maximum accessibility
10. **Corporate** - Professional, business-focused
11. **Minimalist** - Clean, distraction-free

## Using Colors in Code

### CSS Variables

```css
.my-component {
  background-color: hsl(var(--background));
  color: hsl(var(--foreground));
  border: 1px solid hsl(var(--border));
}

.my-component:hover {
  background-color: hsl(var(--accent));
  color: hsl(var(--accent-foreground));
}
```

### Tailwind Classes

```tsx
<div className="bg-background text-foreground border-border">
  <button className="bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/90">
    Primary Button
  </button>
  <button className="bg-secondary text-secondary-foreground hover:bg-secondary/80">
    Secondary Button
  </button>
</div>
```

## Dark Mode

All themes automatically support dark mode. The color system switches based on the `.dark` class:

```tsx
// Theme switcher will toggle this class
<html className="dark">
  {/* All colors automatically adapt */}
</html>
```

## Accessibility

- All color combinations meet WCAG 2.1 Level AA contrast ratios (4.5:1 for normal text, 3:1 for large text)
- High Contrast theme meets WCAG AAA standards (7:1 ratio)
- Focus indicators use the `--ring` color for consistent visibility
- Colors are semantic, not hardcoded, allowing full customization

## Customizing Colors

Override CSS variables in your global styles:

```css
:root {
  --primary: 200 100% 50%; /* Your brand color */
  --primary-foreground: 0 0% 100%;
}

.dark {
  --primary: 200 100% 40%; /* Darker for dark mode */
}
```

